  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Information Technology obligated $79.4M in FY2027 to date across 25 awards, with an average award size of $3.2M. Obligations fell 98.4% year over year compared with recent full years. Fiscal-year obligations in prior full years were much larger: FY22 was $4.1B, FY23 was $4.3B, FY24 was $4.8B, FY25 was $4.6B, and FY26 was $4.9B. The Department of Commerce accounted for most FY2027 to date obligations at $60.5M, followed by the Department of Transportation at $19.3M and the Environmental Protection Agency at $183K. Other Computer Related Services was the largest market by obligations at $60.5M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $18.8M and Environmental Consulting Services at $199K. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity rather than a full year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations drop so much in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 98.4% year over year. Recent full-year totals were FY22 $4.1B, FY23 $4.3B, FY24 $4.8B, FY25 $4.6B, and FY26 $4.9B, compared with FY27 at $79.4M. Concentration of FY2027 to date obligations in a few agencies and markets helps explain the low total: the Department of Commerce obligated $60.5M and Other Computer Related Services accounted for $60.5M. The FY2027 totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets are driving FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce is the top buying agency at $60.5M, followed by the Department of Transportation at $19.3M and the Environmental Protection Agency at $183K. Other Computer Related Services is the top NAICS market at $60.5M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $18.8M and Environmental Consulting Services at $199K."
      }
    ]
  },
